{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1368008-concepts-for-an-investigation-supernal-solar","id":1368008,"title":"Concepts for an Investigation-supernal Solar","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-15T00:55:33-08:00","id":1368008,"title":"Concepts for an Investigation-supernal Solar","content":"Investigation is one of the abilities I use most with any Exalt, I just like investigating stuff.<br /> And I also like the Solar investigation charms, I have most of them on my creepy Zenith monk.<br /> <br /> But for a defining ability... Well, &quot;Solar detective&quot; seems very anachronistic to me. &quot;Solar magistrate&quot; and &quot;Solar inquisitor&quot; seem more fitting for a pre-modern setting. Any other ideas, forumites?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T03:26:04-08:00","id":1368018,"title":"","content":"Bounty hunter perhaps? A prefect? Mercenaries and enforcers also work, as long as your boss is the type to care about you bringing in the guy who <i>actually did it</i> over just having somebody to execute as an example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T08:10:07-08:00","id":1368047,"title":"","content":"Probably still a bit anachronistic, but less so than a detective: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thief-taker\" target=\"_blank\">a thief-taker</a>. And it might not even be all that anachronistic - just the name. I believe that in most societies where law enforcement wasn't an organized job of the state, private citizens would be paid to take up the role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T13:47:07-08:00","id":1368117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1368008-concepts-for-an-investigation-supernal-solar?p=1368047#post1368047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I believe that in most societies where law enforcement wasn't an organized job of the state, private citizens would be paid to take up the role.</div> </div> </div> </div>In pre-industrial societies generally when a crime happens, you either know exactly who did that or you have no slightest chance of finding that out.<br /> <br /> And incidentally, it's rather the former than the latter. Typically, your life is very crowded with people that know you very well. You spend most of your time on your farm where everyone in the vilage gathers. If it's in the city, you spend it, say, in your workshop. If you are an apprentice you also sleep in that workshop with a couple of other apprentices. If you live in the farm, you generally sleep on one bad with the whole family. If you are wealthy, then you are <i>constantly</i> surrounded by your servants. People used to build <i>secret passages</i> to really sneak out of their chambers.<br /> <br /> Oh, and if you want to get by alone? You won't. Preparing your meal, preparing your bad, and general maintenance like that took so much time in the preindustrial era that it was virtually impossible, unless you are a miserable outcast.<br /> <br /> And if you were a miserable outcast? Well, then everyone suspects you when something bad happens and there is generally reason to it. But in the city there are more people like you so good luck finding out who robbed you.<br /> <br /> Of course, you can be a thief in the medieval city, but then generally people that know you will know, but generally you will rather be caught in flagranti then as a result of an investigation.<br /> <br /> Generally, privacy is a very modern thing and detective stories need some privacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-15-2020, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T16:09:37-08:00","id":1368162,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judge_Dee\" target=\"_blank\">Judge Dee</a> would fit right in to Exalted, and the investigating court figure trope is <i>huuuuuge</i> one in Asia. A lot of samurai drama involves a wandering official in disguise, rooting out corruption and righting wrongs, who then pulls out his official mark of the Shogun and arrests everyone. The Shinsengumi are basically samurai cops who investigate anti-government rebels","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}